              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EStoolball is ideal for schools - a team sport adaptable to almost any environment, quick to set up and pack away, easy to learn yet teaching plenty of important skills. That\u0027s why the UK National Curriculum for 2009-11 cited it as a good striking and fielding sport at ages 11-16.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022/{localLink:3441f1ba-e7ca-4274-a486-80e98867c683}\u0022 type=\u0022document\u0022 title=\u0022Starter stoolball\u0022\u003EStarter stoolball\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe 10 essential rules you need to play stoolball, perfect for trying out the sport, leading a school PE lesson, or a quick match in the park. Print them out and stick them to the back of your wicket.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022/{localLink:9289fd26-3f8f-4a4c-b997-1d5fe631e458}\u0022 type=\u0022document\u0022 title=\u0022Key Stage 3 lesson plans\u0022\u003EResources for schools\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThese lesson plans together form a National Curriculum unit of work for pupils at Key Stage 3 (ages 11-14), using stoolball to support key concepts of competence, performance, creativity and healthy active lifestyles. Complete coaching pack for schools.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022/{localLink:dd37ee9f-6dec-4b29-a1eb-bc82e99c1853}\u0022 type=\u0022document\u0022 title=\u0022Coaching in schools\u0022\u003ECoaching in schools\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EStoolball England offers coaching in schools. We are always looking for volunteers or companies to help us coach more schools.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022/{localLink:f5a8c6ee-414d-42bd-89ea-3bb57f4d810a}\u0022 type=\u0022document\u0022 title=\u0022Free equipment from Sainsbury\u2019s Active Kids\u0022\u003EFree equipment from Sainsbury\u2019s Active Kids\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ECollect Active Kids vouchers from Sainsbury\u0027s and ask your local school to invest in stoolball.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003C!--more--\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022/{localLink:2813c29b-aef9-41db-ae53-215dc2178fcb}\u0022 type=\u0022document\u0022 title=\u0022Buy stoolball equipment from Stoolball England\u0022\u003EBuy stoolball equipment from Stoolball England\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EYou can buy approved stoolball bats, balls, wickets and scorebooks from Stoolball England, and DVDs explaining the rules, providing coaching in striking and fielding skills and suggesting practice exercises you can use in lessons.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022/{localLink:6de19ba3-220d-4096-95f7-1249f8638000}\u0022 type=\u0022document\u0022 title=\u0022Promote stoolball and find new players\u0022\u003EPromote stoolball in your school\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EEncourage pupils to get involved in sport by putting up posters at your school, or window stickers in the classroom. Contact nearby teams to ask about building links between them and your school.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022/{localLink:b311f3b6-87b5-40b8-8de0-158781bdfdf1}\u0022 type=\u0022document\u0022 title=\u0022History\u0022\u003EStoolball history\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EStoolball is a very old sport, dating back over 500 years. It has stories relevant to the role of the church in English life, and the rehabilitation of soldiers after World War One. Use the primary and secondary sources in our history section as part of a history lesson.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
